message.content:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   **A. CI failure fix on PR #85** (SFCC-236, `feature/SFCC-236_product-card-shared-component`): Marcel asked me to investigate and plan a fix for the failing "Storybook interaction & a11y tests" GitHub Actions check, then execute per the established zimmerMANNPostBuild-style workflow (investigate → confirm with user → dispatch to zm-implementer → verify → commit/push only on explicit ask).

   **B. PR body correction**: Marcel confirmed the Homepage renders via Contentful (resolving a previously-open question) and explicitly asked me to "update the PR body, remove that flag" for that specific bullet (appearing in two places in the body).

   **C. CodeRabbit review response cycle** on PR #85, following this project's established discipline (verify every finding before acting, "CodeRabbit has run as low as 1-in-6 correct on this repo"): Marcel asked me to (1) verify/validate 3 initial findings before doing anything, (2) report a clear fix/decline breakdown, (3) fix only the valid one, (4) commit it, (5) draft natural-but-technical replies for all 3, (6) remove one specific paragraph from a draft on request, (7) post all 3, then (8) verify and (9) reply to a 4th finding that appeared afterward.

   **D. Major new task — live homepage demo of ZimmProductCard**: Marcel's exact words: "with PR #85 now open, i want to do something more with the work that we did for SFCC-236, here's my vision: to build off the current state of the brancha and render all the variants and state of the product card that uses a live product from SFCC in the current blank homepage to demonstrate it live and to open a draft PR so that a feature-level MRT ENV is spun up and it can be used to showcase the product card in action, let's plan it." He then significantly raised the scope bar: "we want full coverage on this run; working size setting, adding to bag/cart, multiple images, change image on hover, etc. - basically it's a demo of all the variants and states that the ACs + designs + comments are requiring in the individual level." He confirmed via AskUserQuestion that add-to-bag must be **fully real** (actual SFCC basket mutation) and that the demo is **temporary/throwaway** (not intended to merge). He also offered his own running local dev server for testing: "i have a local instance running at port 3000, try to test for SFCC live products there as you need."

   **E. Ongoing debugging** of the implemented demo, driven entirely by Marcel's live browser testing feedback at each step (he has no direct code visibility into my implementation — all diagnosis has come from his reports of what he sees/doesn't see in his browser, plus devtools data he's pasted on request).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Zimmermann PWA Kit override architecture (`overrides/app/...` mirroring `@salesforce/retail-react-app`), Tier 1 (frozenFiles.md)/Tier 2 (protectedFiles.md) file protection, CODEOWNERS as the real enforcement mechanism.
   - `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` hooks: `useProductSearch`, `useProduct`, `useShopperBasketsV2MutationHelper` (aliased `useShopperBasketsMutationHelper`), `useCustomerId`.
   - Real SFCC org for this project's dev tier: `f_ecom_bkzk_002` / `qmyt7hks.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com`, site `ZimmermannAU`.
   - `commerce-sdk-isomorphic`'s `ShopperProductsTypes.Product`/`ProductSearchHit` real field shapes: `imageGroups[].images[].{link,disBaseLink,alt,title}`, `price`/`currency` (plain number/string), `variationAttributes[].{id,values[].{value,name,orderable}}`, `variationValues` (codes only, e.g. `{color:'BLACK'}`), `inventory.orderable`/`variant.orderable` (real stock signal, no `c_isUnavailable` field exists).
   - Base retail-react-app utilities being reused: `filterImageGroups` (`@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/utils/product-utils`, real signature `(imageGroups=[], {viewType, variationValues}) => ImageGroup[]`), `productUrlBuilder` (`@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/utils/url`, `(product) => encodeURI('/product/'+product.id)`).
   - The real add-to-cart chain in this codebase: PDP button → `handleCartItem` (`product-view/index.tsx`) → `handleAddToCart` (`product-detail/index.tsx:507-598`) → `addItemToNewOrExistingBasket(productItems)` from `useShopperBasketsMutationHelper()`; internally handles "no basket yet" automatically; guest-safe via SDK's `auth.ready()`.
   - `ZimmProductCard`'s discriminated union: `ZimmProductCardBaseProps` (common) & `(PlpVariation | HomeVariation | WishlistVariation)`. **Critical**: `home` variation has NO `onAddToBag`/bag button at all (`VARIATION_CONFIG.home.showBag: false`); `colour`/`size` exist only on `WishlistVariation` (required there).
   - `useToast` from base `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-toast` (no override exists) — real precedent: error toast on add-to-cart failure, no success toast for add-to-cart in real PDP (opens a modal instead); wishlist-add's own success toast is the closest reusable precedent.
   - `deploy-preview.yml`: triggers on `push` to `feature/**`/`fix/**` (not `pull_request`), no path filter; every preview points at the same shared `dev`-tier SFCC org; draft PR status changes nothing about any workflow in this repo.
   - `e2e-browserstack-preview.yml` greps PR title+body+branch name for `SFCC-[0-9]+` to decide whether to run BrowserStack/possibly file a Jira defect — informed the decision to keep the new branch/PR name/title/body free of any `SFCC-###` pattern.
   - `HOME_SHOP_PRODUCTS_CATEGORY_ID` (resolves to `'newarrivals'`) is a generic Salesforce reference-storefront sample category — **confirmed via live testing to have zero real hits** in Zimmermann's actual catalog. Fixed by switching to a free-text `q` parameter instead (confirmed real/valid via `commerce-sdk-isomorphic` type defs).
   - This project's ESLint config **enforces `react/react-in-jsx-scope`** (requires explicit `import React from 'react'` in every JSX file) **despite** `tsconfig.json`'s `"jsx": "react-jsx"` setting technically making it unnecessary — a real, confirmed convention I initially got wrong (removed the import, then had to revert after ESLint flagged it).
   - `@typescript-eslint/no-misused-promises`-style issue: passing an `async` function directly to a `() => void`-typed prop (like `onAddToBag`) is flagged by ESLint even though TS's structural typing allows it and try/catch already prevents unhandled rejections — fixed by wrapping: `const handleAddToBag = () => { void handleAddToBagAsync(); };`.
   - Diagnostic methodology correction: a `<script src="pages-home.js">` tag's presence in SSR HTML does NOT indicate the bundle's *content* is fresh (no content-hash in the filename) — must curl the actual bundle file content to verify code changes were picked up, not just the outer HTML shell. Also: the product-search section's data is fetched **client-side post-hydration** with no SSR prefetch, so `curl` (no JS execution) can never see resolved product data — only a real browser can.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`overrides/app/pages/home/liveProductCardDemoMapper.ts`** (NEW, throwaway demo file) — pure mapping functions, no React/react-intl import, mirrors `productInfo.ts`'s injected-formatter pattern. Current full content (post `eslint --fix`, as shown in the last system reminder):
     ```ts
     import { filterImageGroups } from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/utils/product-utils';
     import { productUrlBuilder } from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/utils/url';
     import type {
       ZimmProductCardBaseProps,
       ZimmProductCardImage,
     } from '../../components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard';
     import type { ZimmSizeChipValue } from '../../components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmSizeChipGroup';

     export type LiveDemoImage = { link: string; disBaseLink?: string; alt?: string };
     export type LiveDemoImageGroup = {
       viewType: string;
       variationAttributes?: Array<{ id: string; values?: Array<{ value: string }> }>;
       images: LiveDemoImage[];
     };
     export type LiveDemoVariationAttributeValue = { value: string; name?: string; orderable?: boolean };
     export type LiveDemoVariationAttribute = {
       id: string;
       name?: string;
       values?: LiveDemoVariationAttributeValue[];
     };
     export type LiveDemoVariant = {
       productId: string;
       price?: number;
       orderable?: boolean;
       variationValues?: Record<string, string>;
     };
     export type LiveDemoSourceHit = {
       productId: string;
       productName?: string;
       price?: number;
       currency?: string;
       orderable?: boolean;
       imageGroups?: LiveDemoImageGroup[];
       variationAttributes?: LiveDemoVariationAttribute[];
       variants?: LiveDemoVariant[];
     };

     export type FormatPrice = (amount: number, currency: string) => string;

     const COLOUR_ATTRIBUTE_ID = 'color';
     const SIZE_ATTRIBUTE_ID = 'size';

     export const resolveDemoVariant = (hit: LiveDemoSourceHit) => {
       const variant = hit.variants?.find((v) => v.orderable) ?? hit.variants?.[0];
       return {
         productId: variant?.productId ?? hit.productId,
         price: variant?.price ?? hit.price,
         colourCode: variant?.variationValues?.[COLOUR_ATTRIBUTE_ID],
         sizeCode: variant?.variationValues?.[SIZE_ATTRIBUTE_ID],
       };
     };

     const resolveAttributeName = (hit: LiveDemoSourceHit, attributeId: string, code?: string): string | undefined =>
       hit.variationAttributes?.find((a) => a.id === attributeId)?.values?.find((v) => v.value === code)?.name;

     export type LiveDemoCardBase = {
       base: Pick<
         ZimmProductCardBaseProps,
         'href' | 'name' | 'headingLevel' | 'primaryImage' | 'hoverImage' | 'images' | 'currentPrice'
       >;
       colour?: string;
       size?: string;
       variantProductId: string;
       variantPrice?: number;
     };

     export const selectLiveProductCardBase = (
       hit: LiveDemoSourceHit,
       formatPrice: FormatPrice,
     ): LiveDemoCardBase | null => {
       if (!hit.productName) return null;
       const variant = resolveDemoVariant(hit);
       const colour = resolveAttributeName(hit, COLOUR_ATTRIBUTE_ID, variant.colourCode);
       const size = resolveAttributeName(hit, SIZE_ATTRIBUTE_ID, variant.sizeCode);

       const groups = filterImageGroups(hit.imageGroups ?? [], {
         viewType: 'medium',
         variationValues: variant.colourCode ? { [COLOUR_ATTRIBUTE_ID]: variant.colourCode } : {},
       }) as LiveDemoImageGroup[];
       const groupImages = groups?.[0]?.images ?? [];

       const toCardImage = (img: LiveDemoImage): ZimmProductCardImage => ({
         src: img.disBaseLink || img.link,
         alt: img.alt?.trim() || `${hit.productName}${colour ? `, ${colour}` : ''}`,
       });

       return {
         base: {
           href: productUrlBuilder({ id: hit.productId }),
           name: hit.productName,
           headingLevel: 'h3',
           primaryImage: groupImages[0] ? toCardImage(groupImages[0]) : toCardImage({ link: '', alt: hit.productName }),
           hoverImage: groupImages[1] ? toCardImage(groupImages[1]) : undefined,
           images: groupImages.length > 1 ? groupImages.map(toCardImage) : undefined,
           currentPrice:
             typeof variant.price === 'number' && hit.currency ? formatPrice(variant.price, hit.currency) : undefined,
         },
         colour,
         size,
         variantProductId: variant.productId,
         variantPrice: variant.price,
       };
     };

     export const buildSizeChipValues = (hit: LiveDemoSourceHit): ZimmSizeChipValue[] =>
       (hit.variationAttributes?.find((a) => a.id === SIZE_ATTRIBUTE_ID)?.values ?? []).map((v) => ({
         value: v.value,
         label: v.name ?? v.value,
         isDisabled: v.orderable === false,
       }));

     export const pickDemoHit = (hits: LiveDemoSourceHit[]): LiveDemoSourceHit | undefined => {
       const imageCount = (hit: LiveDemoSourceHit) =>
         (filterImageGroups(hit.imageGroups ?? [], { viewType: 'medium', variationValues: {} }) as LiveDemoImageGroup[])?.[0]
           ?.images?.length ?? 0;
       const sizeCount = (hit: LiveDemoSourceHit) =>
         hit.variationAttributes?.find((a) => a.id === SIZE_ATTRIBUTE_ID)?.values?.length ?? 0;
       return hits.find((h) => imageCount(h) >= 2 && sizeCount(h) >= 2) ?? hits.find((h) => imageCount(h) >= 1) ?? hits[0];
     };
     ```
     **Suspected root cause of "images not loading"**: the `viewType: 'medium'` filter in `selectLiveProductCardBase`/`pickDemoHit` may not match this SFCC org's real image-group `viewType` values, causing `groupImages` to be empty and falling back to `toCardImage({link: '', alt: hit.productName})` — an empty-string `src`. **Not yet confirmed** — waiting on Marcel to share the console output of the raw `imageGroups` diagnostic log.

   - **`overrides/app/pages/home/liveProductCardDemoSection.tsx`** (NEW, throwaway demo file) — the container component. Last known full state includes: real `useProductSearch` call now using `q: 'dress'` + `htype: 'master'` (changed from broken `cgid`-based refine), destructured `isLoading`/`isError`/`error`, two temporary `console.log` diagnostics (`'[live-demo] search state'` and `'[live-demo] raw imageGroups of first hit'`), 4 distinct visible fallback states (loading/error/zero-hits/unusable-hit) replacing the original silent `return null`, the `DemoSizeSelectableCard` wrapper (adapted from Storybook's `LiveSizeSelectionCard`), real `handleAddToBagAsync`/`handleAddToBag` (sync wrapper) using `addItemToNewOrExistingBasket`, `demoNotifyMe`/`demoRemove` toast-only stubs, and the 11-instance array (`Default (PLP)`, `PLP — Out of stock`, `Home`, `Home — Out of stock`, `Wishlist`, `Wishlist — Out of stock`, `Single image`, `Multiple images`, `With sale price`, `One size`, `Loading price`). Import line fixed to multi-line format:
     ```ts
     import React, { useMemo, useState } from 'react';
     import { useIntl } from 'react-intl';
     import { Box, Stack, Text } from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/components/shared/ui';
     import Section from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/components/section';
     import {
       useProductSearch,
       useShopperBasketsV2MutationHelper as useShopperBasketsMutationHelper,
     } from '@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react';
     import { useToast } from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-toast';
     import { HOME_SHOP_PRODUCTS_LIMIT } from '../../constants';
     ```
     The `handleAddToBag` fix applied:
     ```ts
     const handleAddToBagAsync = async () => {
       if (!demoProduct) return;
       try {
         await addItemToNewOrExistingBasket([
           { productId: demoProduct.variantProductId, price: demoProduct.variantPrice, quantity: 1 },
         ]);
         showToast({ title: 'Added to bag', status: 'success' });
       } catch (error) {
         showToast({
           title: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Could not add to bag',
           status: 'error',
         });
       }
     };
     const handleAddToBag = () => {
       void handleAddToBagAsync();
     };
     ```
     The `instances` array formatting was fixed to multi-line objects for the previously-flagged entries (PLP/Home/Wishlist Out-of-stock, Single image).

   - **`overrides/app/pages/home/index.tsx`** (MODIFIED, base file) — 2 additions only: import of `LiveProductCardDemoSection`, and an unconditional `<LiveProductCardDemoSection />` render line placed directly in the top-level `Home` component, **before** the Contentful-gated `{entryId ? <HomePreviewContent .../> : <HomeNormal />}` branch. This placement was a self-corrected fix from the Plan agent's original (wrong) suggestion to mount inside `HomepageContent`, which I confirmed by direct file read is itself still gated behind `HomeNormal`'s `if (!homepageContent) return null` check.

   - **`/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/.claude/plans/serialized-bubbling-snowflake.md`** — overwritten with the full "Live ZimmProductCard homepage demo" plan (approved by Marcel via ExitPlanMode). Contains the 7-section approach (branch strategy, mapper design, 11-instance table, add-to-bag wiring, size-selection wrapper, corrected homepage wiring, PR body draft), known gaps list, and verification steps. Explicitly states: "this plan's own git-push and `gh pr create` steps (§1, §7) are outward-facing actions — implement and verify the code first, then pause for a separate, explicit go before pushing or opening the PR."

   - **PR #85 body** (`gh pr edit 85`) — edited to remove the "Whether Homepage is genuinely SFCC-rendered or Contentful-driven" bullet from both the Description and Known-gaps sections, per Marcel's direct instruction.

   - **`postbuild.md`** (`~/Dev/zimmerMANN-skills/.runs/SFCC-236/postbuild.md`) — updated with a dated resolution note for the Homepage/Contentful question (struck through the old open-question text, added "RESOLVED 2026-09-05 (Marcel): Homepage is via Contentful" with the real consequence noted: the `home` variation has no current real SFCC-side caller).

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **CI axe failure on `WithSalePrice` stories**: root-caused to a pre-existing, deliberately-accepted design/accessibility trade-off (Figma's own `#969696` token fails AA contrast) that had an established suppression pattern my new stories didn't replicate. Fixed by adding `parameters: { a11y: { test: 'off' } }` + matching comment to both new `WithSalePrice` stories, mirroring the exact existing pattern. Verified via a full local `build-storybook` → `http-server` (isolated port 6007, not touching the peer session's live instance on 6006) → `test-storybook --ci` run: all 44 suites/209 tests passed.
   - **CodeRabbit finding #2 (bare `.focus()`)**: confirmed valid via direct code comparison with the sibling test; fixed via zm-implementer dispatch (async test, `userEvent.setup()`, `await user.tab()`, intermediate `toHaveFocus()` assertion); verified independently (diff exactly matched spec, tsc/tests clean).
   - **My own investigation methodology error**: initially concluded the dev server hadn't picked up new files by checking only the outer HTML shell (script tag references), which can never reveal whether a non-hashed bundle filename's *content* changed. Self-corrected by fetching `pages-home.js`'s actual content directly and finding 12 real matches for my new code — proving the build was fine all along and my earlier "not picked up" conclusion was wrong.
   - **`HOME_SHOP_PRODUCTS_CATEGORY_ID` ('newarrivals') returns zero real hits**: confirmed live via Marcel's browser testing (matches a risk I had flagged but not confirmed during planning). Fixed by switching the demo's own search call from `cgid`-based refine to a free-text `q: 'dress'` parameter (confirmed valid via SDK type defs), removing the now-unused import. Verified the fix was picked up via hot-reload (no restart needed) by re-fetching the bundle and finding `'dress'` present.
   - **Images not loading (UNRESOLVED)**: cards now render with real name/price/size-chip data, but images are blank. Added diagnostic logging (`console.log('[live-demo] raw imageGroups of first hit', ...)`) to inspect real data shape before attempting a fix — **still waiting on Marcel to report the console output**; he only replied "images are still not loading" without yet providing the requested data.
   - **Incorrectly removed `React` import**: removed it as apparently-unused (per a naive TS "declared but never read" hint), which broke ESLint's `react/react-in-jsx-scope` rule (14 errors). Reverted — confirmed via direct ESLint run that this project's lint config genuinely requires it despite `tsconfig.json`'s `"jsx": "react-jsx"` setting.
   - **Prettier/formatting lint errors** (multi-line imports, multi-line object literals) in both new files — fixed via manual edits and one `eslint --fix` run (mapper file only).
   - **`no-misused-promises`-style issue**: `onAddToBag`/`onRemove` props (typed `() => void`) were receiving an `async` function directly. Fixed by renaming to `handleAddToBagAsync` and wrapping in a new sync `handleAddToBag = () => { void handleAddToBagAsync(); }`.

5. Problem Solving:
   - Systematically distinguished pre-existing/unrelated errors (Contentful 400 on the homepage's own existing entry fetch, Shopper Context 404) from the actual relevant one (product search), preventing a wrong diagnosis chase.
   - Used a self-built visible-error-state pattern (loading/error/zero-hits/unusable-hit) directly on the page, in preference to continuing a slow multi-round "check devtools, report back" cycle — this successfully surfaced the `HOME_SHOP_PRODUCTS_CATEGORY_ID` root cause in one round.
   - Currently applying the same philosophy to the images issue (added a raw-data console log) but do not yet have the data back.

6. All user messages (verbatim, chronological, excluding tool/system results, this session segment only):
   - "Storybook interaction & a11y tests failed, investigate and let's plan to resolve it"
   - (AskUserQuestion answer) "Replicate the existing suppression (Recommended)"
   - "commit and push"
   - "with PR #85 now open... it's via contentful, update the PR body, remove that flag" [full text in prior turn]
   - "3 coderabbit change requests/comments, let's go for verification and validation of CRs claims first before resolve/comment-reply"
   - "so what's the coderabbt resolve looking like? what's to fix? what's to just post a reply to? what's what?"
   - "make the fix first, then report back when done"
   - "commit this"
   - "let's prepare the replies, for the replies natural human language without losing the technical aspect and value"
   - "remove: Also worth flagging: this thread shows \"✅ Addressed in commit 1fdb356\" — I checked, and that's not accurate, the row is still malformed as of the latest push. Not fixing it here since the bug lives in the generator script, not in anything this PR authored — raising it as its own ticket against whoever owns that script instead."
   - "post all three now"
   - "a 4th finding was raised, v&v it"
   - "prepare the reply for the 4th finding"
   - "post it"
   - "with PR #85 now open, i want to do something more with the work that we did for SFCC-236, here's my vision: to build off the current state of the brancha and render all the variants and state of the product card that uses a live product from SFCC in the current blank homepage to demonstrate it live and to open a draft PR so that a feature-level MRT ENV is spun up and it can be used to showcase the product card in action, let's plan it"
   - "we want full coverage on this run; working size setting, adding to bag/cart, multiple images, change image on hover, etc. - basically it's a demo of all the variants and states that the ACs + designs + comments are requiring in the individual level"
   - "i have a local instance running at port 3000, try to test for SFCC live products there as you need"
   - (AskUserQuestion answers) "Fully real (Recommended)" and "Temporary / throwaway (Recommended)"
   - (ExitPlanMode approval — no separate text message, plan approved directly)
   - "i checked, nothing appears on the home screen"
   - "restart done, still nothing showing"
   - [pasted two full HTTP request/response header dumps for a 404 Shopper Context API call and a 400 Contentful entries API call]
   - "cards are showing, images are not"
   - "images are still not loading"

7. Pending Tasks:
   - **Diagnose and fix the "images not loading" issue** — waiting on Marcel to share the console output of `[live-demo] raw imageGroups of first hit`, or further investigation once that data (or equivalent) is available.
   - Once images work, continue the plan's own verification steps: confirm hover-swap works, size-chip selection works, at least one real "Add to bag" click produces a real toast + real basket line item.
   - Clean up the temporary diagnostic `console.log` calls and the 4 visible fallback states (loading/error/zero-hits/unusable-hit) — these were added purely for debugging and should likely be simplified/removed once the demo is confirmed working, though this hasn't been explicitly requested yet and the demo is throwaway so some diagnostic scaffolding may be acceptable to leave.
   - Push the branch and open the draft PR — **explicitly gated on a separate, future "go" from Marcel**, per the plan's own stated stop point and this session's consistent practice. Not yet requested.
   - Two smaller, previously-surfaced-but-not-yet-actioned items from the CodeRabbit thread (mentioned to Marcel, no response yet): whether to manually resolve the GitHub thread CodeRabbit couldn't auto-resolve, and whether CodeRabbit should be asked to file a GitHub issue for the registry-generator bug.

8. Current Work:
   Immediately before this summary request, I was in the middle of cleaning up ESLint/prettier findings in the two new demo files, triggered by IDE diagnostics that appeared after my fixes for the "images not loading" investigation. The exact sequence: I ran `npx eslint --resolve-plugins-relative-to node_modules/@salesforce/pwa-kit-dev --fix overrides/app/pages/home/liveProductCardDemoMapper.ts`, confirmed it reduced findings to just 1 pre-existing warning (`Invalid type "string | undefined" of template literal expression` at line 102, non-blocking), then ran `npx tsc --noEmit` to do a final full re-verification — this command's tool result included a system-generated notice: "[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: overrides/app/pages/home/liveProductCardDemoMapper.ts. Call Read before editing.]" (referring to the `--fix` command's own modification, not a new issue), followed immediately by a system reminder showing the mapper file's current full post-fix content (reproduced verbatim in section 3 above). I had not yet reported this lint-cleanup completion back to Marcel, and had not yet returned to the primary unresolved issue (images not loading — still waiting on the raw `imageGroups` console data he was asked for two messages prior). No git commit has been made on the `feature/zimmproductcard-live-demo` branch yet — all work (the two new files, the `home/index.tsx` edit, and all debugging fixes) remains uncommitted in the working tree.

9. Optional Next Step:
   Report back to Marcel that the lint/formatting cleanup is complete (`tsc` clean, ESLint clean apart from one pre-existing non-blocking warning), and re-ask for the specific diagnostic data still needed to resolve the open "images not loading" issue — the console output of `[live-demo] raw imageGroups of first hit]`, which was requested in my message right before his "images are still not loading" reply: "Could you open the browser console and paste what `[live-demo] raw imageGroups of first hit` logged? That'll show the real `viewType` values and image URLs this org returns, which is exactly what decides whether my `viewType: 'medium'` filter is matching anything." This is the direct, explicit next step in the active debugging thread and should not be skipped or assumed — no code changes to the image-resolution logic should be made until that real data is seen, consistent with the "prove it, don't guess" pattern already established twice in this same debugging session (the category-ID fix and the bundle-verification correction).

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/.claude/projects/-Users-marcel-a-n-navarro-Dev-zimmermann-pwa/0b6b5219-f79f-4f3b-a6c2-46afb1c1b554.jsonl
Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with "I'll continue" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.

